[#:seon.task{:name "one-weighted-cache-under-a-memory-cap"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "About fifteen defonce caches each carry a code-constant entry bound and no byte cap (seon.db arity-commit 92.6 MB, projection 12.8 MB, arity-base 9.0 MB; seon.sci.eval base-context 27.4 MB, program-identity, refusal-recording; seon.test.runner reach-holders 16.7 MB; the build-projection memos). Owner rulings: every cache configurable, a library not a hand-rolled cache, one fixed memory cap. Recommended: one Caffeine cache keyed [cache-id key] with maximumWeight from one byte dial and a weigher recorded at insert (~60 lines, roughly net neutral)."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection seon.sci.eval/base-ctx seon.test.runner/reach-memberships}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/mem-idle-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "cache-weights-charge-values-not-keys-and-keep-only-reusable-entries"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Two kinds remain after 5218b097e (task-basis, tasks-tx, derivation-world weigh their values). (1) `:seon.fn/population-targets` (`seon.fn/population-targets`) charges `seon.schema/declaration-projection-bytes-per-form` times `(count forms)` and `:seon.cluster/branch-attribute-changes` (`seon.cluster/branch-declaration-changes`) charges the same per installed and declared attribute, but `forms`, `installed` and `declarations` are the lookup's key, shared with the projection already charged under :seon.schema/declaration-projection; the value is a map of target symbols or a vector of attribute idents. Charge the value's own count, as `seon.task/task-basis-weight` does. (2) `:seon.sci.eval/loaded-digests` (`seon.sci.eval/loaded-digests`) keeps `seon.sci.eval/function-digests` over all ~6,500 functions per commit (256 B each, 10 MB for six entries, 2 hits in 8 lookups on default 2026-10-12, restart-audit/cache-hits.md §3) for every branch commit that `seon.sci.eval/derive-overlay-plan` asks about, and the next defn is a new commit that never hits; the digests of a branch commit are not cached (the task `seon.sci.eval/an-overlay-plan-digests-only-the-authored-rows` removes the call, this one keeps the kind to the loaded commit). Done when `seon.cache-test/population-targets-and-branch-attribute-changes-weigh-their-values` is green: it runs `seon.fn/population-targets` over a fixture projection and `seon.cluster/branch-declaration-changes` on a branch, and asserts through `seon.cache/status` that each kind's charged bytes are within 2x of the value's own size (a data assertion on the status map, the way `seon.cache-test/a-kinds-weight-counts-its-value-not-its-key` does for the other three kinds)."
             :must-read #{seon.fn/population-targets seon.cluster/branch-declaration-changes seon.sci.eval/loaded-digests seon.sci.eval/derive-overlay-plan seon.cache/lookup seon.cache/status seon.schema/declaration-projection-bytes-per-form}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/restart-audit/cache-hits.md"}}]
